= Introduction

Thermoelectric coolers are useful in laboratory and embedded setups where a
compact actuator must maintain a controlled temperature difference across a
small device or sensor assembly @riffat-ma-2003. In practice, the quality of
the final operating point depends both on the thermal behaviour of the module
and on the measurement procedure used to estimate the cold-side temperature
@nist-thermoelectric-measurements.

This starter document keeps the content intentionally small. Its purpose is to
show a realistic thesis structure for WEII while leaving the actual scientific
scope, chapter breakdown, and research narrative to the author.

The second chapter uses one experimental plot, one table, and one listing to
demonstrate the float layout and bibliography workflow of the package. The
references are split into scientific and online sources, which makes it easy to
keep standards, vendor documentation, and research papers separated in the
final thesis.
]
